$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM (3R)-3-hydroxy-2,2-dimethylhex-4-enoic acid methyl ester (12). To a
solution of N-Ts-D-Valine (26.5 g, 97.5 mmol) in dichloromethane (900 mL)
at 0 °C was added dropwise a solution of borane (1.0 M in THF, 97.5 mL,
97.5 mmol). The resulting solution was stirred for 30 min at 0 °C then
cooled to -78 °C. Crotonaldehyde (20.7 g, 293 mmol, 24.5 mL) in
dichloromethane (40 mL) was injected followed by a solution of silyl
ketene acetal 11 (17.0 g, 97.5 mmol) in dichloromethane (40 mL). The
resulting mixture was stirred at -78 °C for 6 h, treated with 10% HCl
(300 mL), allowed to warm to rt, and stirred for an additional 2H. The
mixture was washed with EtOAc (4 × 300 mL). The organic layers were
combined, washed with H2O (200 mL), saturated aqueous NaHCO3 (200 mL),
and brine (100 mL), dried (MgSO4) and concentrated under reduced pressure
to afford the crude product that was further purified by chromatography
on SiO2 (1:8, EtOAc/Hexanes) to provide 13.2 g (79%) of alcohol 12 as a
clear, colorless oil in 93% ee (chiral HPLC (Varian Star) with a DAICEL
00 column; 95:5, hexanes/iPrOH, 1.0 mL/min, UV detection at 210 nm. Rt
5.60 min (major), 7.89 min (minor)): [α]D -13.3 (c 1.2, CH2Cl2, 24 °C);
Rf = 0.46 (EtOAc/hexane, 1:4); 1H NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3) δ 5.72 (app dq, J=
15.3Hz, 6.3Hz, 1H), 5.46 (ddd, J= 15.3Hz, 7.5 Hz, 1.5 Hz, 1H), 4.15-4.05
(m, 1H), 3.70 (s, 3H), 2.56 (bd, J= 5.4 Hz, OH), 1.71 (dd, J= 6.3Hz,
1.2Hz, 3H), 1.16 (2s, 6H); 13C NMR (75 MHz, CDCl3) δ 177.8 129.3, 129.0,
n.7, 51.7, 46.7, 22.3, 19.7, 17.6; IR (neat, cm-1) 3498, 2974, 2948,
1718, 1433, 1267, 1085; HRMS (EI) m/z calcd for C9H16O3 172.1099, found
172.1098.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Total Synthesis of (-)-CP2-Disorazole C1
