$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM a) Step-wise allylation and hydrostannation reaction of
4-ethynylbenzaldehyde (6). 4-Ethynylbenzaldehyde (6) (130 mg, 1 mmol) was
dissolved in toluene (1 mL) in a round-bottom flask and the mixture was
cooled to -35°C. Allylstannane (2a) (0.31 mL, 1 mmol) was added followed
by BF3·OEt2 (0.13 mL, 1.05 equiv). The reaction was monitored until
complete (30 minutes). 2 mL of water were added to quench the reaction.
The organic phase was separated and the aqueous phase was extracted with
CH2Cl2 (3 × 2 mL). Organic phase were combined, dried with MgSO4 and
evaporated using a rotary evaporator. The crude product was subjected to
column chromatography [silica gel; 80:20 hexane/EtOAc, 1% Et3N].
1-(4-ethynylphenyl)but-3-en-1-ol (S24) (148.4 mg, 86%) as a clear oil. IR
(neat): 3292 cm-1. 1H-NMR (500 MHz, CDCl3) δ (ppm) = 2.20 (s, br, 1H),
2.41-2.49 (m, 2H), 3.05 (s, 1H), 4.68-4.71 (dd, J = 8.0, 5.0Hz, 1H),
5.11-5.15 (m, 2H), 5.70-5.79 (m, 1H), 7.27-7.29 (d, J = 8.5 Hz, 2H),
7.44-7.46 (d, J = 8.5 Hz, 2H). 13C NMR (125 MHz, CDCl3) δ (ppm) = 43.6,
72.7, 77.1, 83.4, 118.7, 121.1, 125.7, 132.1, 133.9, 144.5. HRMS (ESI)
m/z calcd for C12H13O [M+H]+, 173.0966; found: 173.0974.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM A One-Pot Allylation-Hydrostannation Sequence with Recycling of the
Intermediate Tin Waste
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Ghosh, Banibrata; Amado-Sierra, Maria Del Rosario I.; Holmes, Daniel;
Maleczka, Robert E. Jr.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Organic Letters (2014), 16(9), 2318-2321

