$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: (b) Typical Procedure for the Addition in
THF-d8. To 1 mL of 1.5 M PhLi in THF-d8 99% was added 66 mg (0.5 mmol) of
(E)-cinnamaldehyde, and the mixtures was allowed to react for 7 h and
then quenched with excess of D2O. The organic layer was dried with
Na2SO4, and a determination procedure similar to that described in (a)
above gave 70% yield of compound 5a-d3.
(E)-2-Methyl-1,3-diphenyl-2-propen-1-ol (3b). Oil. Yield: 76%.
(E)-2-Methyl-1,3-diphenyl-propenone (4b). Oil. Yield: 11%. 5b: 10%. 1H
NMR (500 MHz, CDCl3) δ 1.74 (d, 3H, J) 1.3 Hz), 5.29 (s, 1H), 6.78 (s,
1H), 7.21 (m, 1H), 7.32 (m, 7H), 7.44 (dd, 2H, J) 1.0 and 7.7 Hz). 13C
NMR (125 MHz, CDCl3) δ 13.92, 79.34, 125.84, 126.40, 127.41, 128.02,
128.28, 128.95, 137.50, 139.62, 142.17. HRMS m/z for C16H16O calcd
224.1201, found 224.1205. 1H NMR (200 MHz, CDCl3) δ 1.93 (s, 3H), 7.26
(m, 3H), 7.54 (m, 5H), 7.69 (s, 1H), 7.90 (d, 2H, J= 7.4 Hz). 13C NMR
(125 MHz, CDCl3) δ 14.30, 126.82, 128.55, 128.75, 129.90, 130.58, 131.23,
134.85, 136.03, 139.90, 200.09. HRMS m/z for C16H14O calcd 222.1045,
found 222.1050.
