$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: (Sup1):
(±)-(3E)-1-Chloro-4-phenylbut-3-en-2-ol (General Procedure):- A 250 mL
round bottom flask was flame dried under a stream of nitrogen and allowed
to cool to room temperature. It was then charged with
trans-cinnamaldehyde (4.76 mL, 37.8 mmol) and THF (75 mL). The reaction
mixture was cooled to -78°C and chloroiodomethane (4.13 mL, 56.7 mmol)
was added followed by the slow addition of nBuLi (1.6 M, 23.6 mL, 56.7
mmol) over 30 minutes. The reaction was maintained at -78°C and monitored
by TLC. After 1 hour approximately an equal volume of NH4Claq was added
and the reaction mixture warmed to room temperature. The reaction
contents were transferred to a separatory funnel with ether and the
organic layer isolated. The aqueous layer was extracted with ether, the
combined organics dried with MgSO4, filtered and concentrated in vacuo.
The crude residue was purified by flash chromatography (10 to 12.5%
EtOAc/Hex) to afford the product as a colorless oil.
(±)-(3E)-1-Chloro-3-methyl-4-phenylbut-3-en-2-ol (Sup21) as a colorless
oil, yield 87%. Rf = 0.37 (33% EtOAc/Hex).
