$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: B) Representative Procedure for the Formation
of Chlorohydrins A round bottom flask was torched under a stream of
nitrogen and then charged with an α,β-unsaturated aldehyde and freshly
distilled THF (0.5 M). The resulting solution was cooled to -78 °C and
chloroiodomethane (1.5 eq) was added followed by the slow addition of
n-BuLi (1.5 eq, 1.6 M solution in hexanes) over 30 minutes. The reaction
was maintained at -78 °C and monitored by TLC. When the starting material
had been consumed (~ 1 h) the reaction was quenched with NH4Cl(aq) and
warmed to room temperature. It was transferred to a separatory funnel
with ether and additional NH4Cl(aq) and the organic layer isolated. The
aqueous layer was back-extracted with ether (1x), the organics combined
and dried with magnesium sulfate. The solvent was removed in vacuo and
the residue purified by flash chromatography.
(+/-)-(3E)-1-Chloro-3-methyl-4-phenyl-but-3-en-2-ol Prepared following B,
and purified by flash chromatography (5 Hex : 1 EtOAc). The isolated
product was a colorless oil (yield = 87%). Rf = 0.37 (3 Hex : 1 EtOAc);
1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.41 - 7.36 (m, 2H), 7.33 - 7.26 (m, 3H), 6.67
(s, 1H), 4.46 - 4.39 (m, 1H), 3.75 (dd, J = 11.2 Hz, J = 3.6 Hz, 1H),
3.67 (dd, J = 11.2 Hz, J = 8.0 Hz, 1H), 2.90 (d, J = 3.2 Hz, 1H), 1.92
(d, J = 0.9 Hz, 3H); 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3) δ 137.27, 136.29, 129.32,
128.49, 128.08, 127.12, 77.29, 48.82, 14.28; FTIR (neat) v 3385, 3055,
3024, 2958, 1954, 1887, 1599, 1491, 1445, 1251, 1184, 1075, 1009, 921,
875, 746, 699 cm-1; HRMS (m/z) calculated for C11H13ClO 196.0655, found
196.0662.
