$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: 4. Double Allylboration Reactions of 9. (a)
Synthesis of (E)-1,5-syn-diol (13) as reference. (c) Synthesis of
(E)-1,5-syn-diol (14) as a reference.
(3R,4E,7S)-1,9-diphenylnon-4-ene-3,7-diol (14). 1,5-Diol 14 was
synthesized by using the procedure described above for the synthesis of
13. The crude product was purified by flash column chromatography (SiO2,
hexanes / ethyl acetate, gradient elution: 7:3 to 6:4 to 1:1) to afford
(E)-1,5-syndiol 14 (86% yield) as a white solid. [α]D25 = -6.4 (c 0.64,
CHCl3); ee 96%; 1H (400 MHz, CDCl3) 7.21-7.08 (m, 10H), 5.61-5.49 (m,
2H), 4.01 (q, J = 6.8 Hz, 1H), 3.60-3.54 (m, 1H), 2.75-2.67 (m, 1H),
2.64-2.54 (m, 3H), 2.24-2.18 (m, 1H), 2.11-2.04 (m, 1H), 1.84-1.67 (m,
4H); 13C (100 MHz, CDCl3) 142.0, 141.9, 136.5, 128.44, 128.40, 127.8,
125.88, 125.85, 72.1, 70.3, 40.5, 38.7, 38.6, 32.0, 31.8; IR (neat) 3347,
3084, 3061, 3025, 2924, 2857, 1668, 1602, 1495, 1454, 1312, 1051, 1030,
971, 923, 746, 698 cm-1; HRMS (ESI) calcd for C21H26O2Na [M+Na]+
333.1831, found 333.1822.
