$DATUM 75-85-4
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Right alkyne 24: To a solution of indium (467 mg, 4.08 mmol, 2 eq),
chiral aminoalcohol 25 (868 mg, 4.08 mmol, 2 eq) and pyridine (330 μL,
4.08 mmol, 2 eq) in THF (24.5 mL) under argon at RT was slowly added
propargyl bromide (450 μL, 4.08 mmol, 2 eq). The cloudy suspension was
stirred for 30 min with formation of a coin of indium. Then, more indium
(233 mg, 2.04 mmol, 1 eq) was added and the reaction was cooled to -78°C.
A solution of aldehyde 23 (342 mg, 2.04 mmol, 1 eq) in THF (5 mL) was
added dropwise and the reaction was stirred for 15 h at -78°C then 6 h
during a slow warming to RT. Reaction was quenched with an aqueous 1M
solution of HCl (16 mL). The aqueous layer was extracted with a 1/1
mixture of petrol ether/Et2O (2 x 60 mL). The combined organic extracts
were dried over MgSO4, filtered and concentrated under vacuo.
Purification of the resulting crude yellow oil by flash chromatography
(petrol ether/Et2O 2/1) gave a 82/18 mixture enriched in enantiomer 24 as
a yellow oil (394 mg, 93%). To a solution of this 82/18 mixture of 24
(365 mg, 1.75 mmol, 1 eq) and Et3N (49 μL, 0.35 mmol, 0.2 eq) in
t-amylalcohol (3.5 mL) under air atmosphere at RT was added the DMAP iron
catalyst 26 (58 mg, 0.09 mmol, 5 mol%). After sonication for 10 min to
get a cloudy purple solution, Ac2O was added slowly at 0°C. Then,
reaction was stirred 48 h at 0°C and finally quenched with MeOH (80 μL).
Volatiles were removed under vacuo. Purification of the resulting crude
purple oil by flash chromatography (petrol ether/Et2O 7/3) gave a 95/5
enriched mixture of the enantiomer 24 as a pale yellow oil (280 mg, 81%).
Rf = 0.4 (petrol ether/Et2O 1/1); [α]D = -36.4 (c= 0.55 in CHCl3, 25°C);
1H NMR (400 MHz): 7.49 (d, J = 12.0 Hz, 1H, H-3), 6.25 (d, J = 12.0 Hz,
1H, H-4), 5.01 (d, J = 7.9, 5.7 Hz, 1H, H-6), 3.77 (s, 3H, OCH3 ester),
2.57 (ddd, J = 16.6, 7.9, 2.6 Hz, 1H, H-7a), 2.43 (ddd, J = 16.6, 5.7,
2.6 Hz, 1H, H-7b), 2.08 (t, J = 2.6 Hz, 1H, H-9), 1.94 (s, 6H, H-1’ and
H-2’); 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3): 169.0 (C-1), 145.5 (C-2), 131.9 (C-3),
127.0 (C-5), 123.4 (C-4), 80.2 (C-8), 71.3 (C-9), 68.2 (C-6), 51.9 (OCH3
ester), 26.1 (C-7), 18.8 (C-2’), 12.4 (C-1’); IR (film) ν (max): 3447,
3306, 2951, 1697, 1635, 1603, 1436, 1389, 1322, 1255, 1209, 1112, 1044,
1012, 913, 752, 731; HRMS (ESI+): m/z: calcd for C12H16O3Na [M+Na]+:
231.0997; found: 231.1007.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, 95:5 diastereomeric mixture, slow addition of propargyl
bromide stage 1, aldehyde stage 2 and acetic anhydride stage 5,
additional indium added before cooling stage 1
