$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Representative procedure for the preparation
of allylic alcohols (allylic alcohol S3): To flame-dried magnesium
turnings (4.05 g, 0.167 mol) and iodine (a crystal) was added THF (33
mL). Once this mixture was cooled (0°C), 3-chloro-2-methyl-1-propene (2.2
mL, 23 mmol) was added dropwise. The reaction mixture was warmed to
ambient temperature for 1.5 h and then was transferred by cannula to
another flask. To the cooled (0°C) Grignard reagent was added
phenylacetaldehyde (1.9 mL, 17 mmol) dropwise over 5 min. The reaction
mixture was warmed to ambient temperature. After 2.5 h, H2O (25 mL) and
brine (25 mL) were added, and the aqueous layer was extracted with Et2O
(3 x 30 mL). The combined organic layers were dried over Na2SO4 and
concentrated in vacuo. Allylic alcohol S15: Following the representative
procedure for the preparation of allylic alcohols, to a solution of
magnesium turnings (10.1 g, 416 mmol) and iodine in THF (42 mL) was added
3-chloro-2-methylpropene (5.5 mL, 56 mmol). To this solution was added
p-tolualdehyde (5.0 mL, 42 mmol). S15 as a colorless oil that was used
without further purification (7.12 g, 97% unpurified yield). The spectral
data are consistent with the data reported:16 1H NMR (600 MHz, CDCl3) δ
7.28 (d, J = 8.1, 2H), 7.16 (d, J = 7.8, 2H), 4.92-4.91 (m, 1H),
4.85-4.84 (m, 1H), 4.78 (dd, J = 8.6, 4.9, 1H), 2.42 (dd, J = 8.6, 0.9,
1H), 2.42-2.41 (m, 1H), 2.34 (s, 3H), 2.07 (br s, 1H), 1.79 (s, 3H); 13C
NMR (150 MHz, CDCl3) δ 142.6 (C), 141.2 (C), 137.2 (C), 129.2 (CH), 125.9
(CH), 114.1 (CH2), 71.4 (CH), 48.4 (CH2), 22.5 (CH3), 21.2 (CH3).
