$DATUM (3R,4R,5E,7S)-3,5,7-Trimethyl-9-phenyl-1,5-nonadien-4-ol (5). To a
stirring-78 °C solution of tBuOK in THF (15.3 mL, 1.0 M in THF, 15.3
mmol) was added viacannula trans-2-butene (3.45 mL, 30.6 mmol) followed
by the addition of nBuLi (6.13mL, 2.5 M in hexanes, 15.3 mmol). The
resulting orange solution was stirred for 25 min.at -45 °C then cooled
back to -78 °C and (+)-Ipc2BOMe (5.82 g, 18.4 mmol) in ether(18.4 mL) was
added. The resulting colorless solution was stirred for 30 min.
andBF3.Et2O (2.64 mL, 20.8 mmol) was added. The mixture was stirred for 5
min. followedby the addition of
(2E,4S)-2,4-dimethyl-6-phenyl-2-hexen-1-al (7) (2.48 g, 12.3 mmol)
inether (18.3 mL) via cannula. The mixture was stirred for 15 h at -78
°C, and satd. NaOAc(8.2 mL) and 30 % H2O2 (8.2 mL) were added. After
being stirred for 15 h at 23 °C, themixture was diluted with ether and
washed with brine. The separated aq. layer wasextracted with CH2Cl2. The
combined organic layers were dried over MgSO4 andconcentrated. Flash
chromatography (silica gel, ethyl acetate/ hexanes = 1/25) gave thetitle
compound (5) (2.53 g, 80 %) as a clear oil (>99% diastereomerically
pure):. 1H NMR(300 MHz, CDCl3) δ 0.95 (d, J = 6.9 Hz, 3 H), 1.02 (d, J =
6.6 Hz, 3 H), 1.55-1.8 (m, 2H), 1.64 (d, J = 1.2 Hz, 3 H), 1.78 (s, 1 H),
2.3-2.45 (m, 1 H), 2.4-2.55 (m, 1 H), 2.6-2.75(m, 2 H), 3.70 (d, J = 8.7
Hz, 1 H), 5.15-5.3 (m, 3 H), 5.75-5.9 (m, 1 H), 7.2-7.35 (m, 5H); 13C NMR
(75 MHz, CDCl3) δ 11.28, 16.76, 20.90, 31.69, 33.79, 39.08, 42.03,
81.15,116.15, 125.46, 128.12 (2 C), 128.28 (2 C), 133.81, 134.66, 141.15,
142.61.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, key intermediate, Brown's asymmetric crotylboration,
in-situ generated reactant
