$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure A. Alkyne Addition to
Unsaturated Aldehydes To an oven-dried round-bottomed flask under N2
atmosphere was added ZnBr2 (104 mg, 0.398 mmol). The flask was charged
with Et2O, then alkyne (2.0 mmol), diisopropylethylamine (700 μL, 519 mg,
4.01 mmol), aldehyde (4.0 mmol), and TMSOTf (432 μL, 530 mg, 2.39 mmol)
were added sequentially. The heterogeneous mixture was stirred for 1 h,
then passed through a filter of silica (1.0 cm x 3.0 cm) with Et2O. The
mixture was concentrated in vacuo, then dissolved in THF (6 mL). The
solution was stirred with 1.0 M HCl (3 mL) for 15 min, then diluted in
Et2O and washed with water (1x) and saturated NaHCO3 (1x). The organic
layer was diluted with hexanes (1:2 hexanes:Et2O) and dried over Na2SO4.
The solvent was removed in vacuo and the residue was purified by column
chromatography (5-20% EtOAc/hexanes).
(1E)-2-Methyl-1,5-diphenylpent-1-en-4-yn-3-ol (9) The title compound was
prepared according to General Procedure A, using phenylacetylene (220 μL,
205 mg, 2.00 mmol) as the alkyne and α -methylcinnamaldehyde (560 μL, 586
mg, 4.01 mmol) as the aldehyde. The product was isolated as a yellow oil
(94% yield): IR (film) 3328, 3056, 2905, 2847, 1592, 1487, 1433, 1355,
1258, 1177, 1064, 986, 913, 862, 753 cm-1; 1H NMR (500 MHz, CDCl3) δ
7.51-7.48 (m, 2H), 7.40-7.33 (m, 7H), 7.29-7.25 (m, 1H), 6.80 (s, 1H),
5.18 (d, J = 5.6 Hz, 1H), 2.11-2.08 (m, 4H); 13C NMR (125 MHz, CDCl3) δ
137.2, 136.8, 131.8, 129.0, 128.6, 128.3, 128.2, 127.3, 126.8, 122.5,
88.1, 86.4, 68.9, 14.2; HRMS (ESI): Exact mass calcd for C18H16ONa
[M+Na]+, 271.1093. Found 271.1082.
