$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Ethyl 2-bydroxy-4-[(1,1-dimethylethyl) dimethylsilyloxy]-3-pentenoate
(5a): Vinyl iodide 4a (2.70 g, 9.00 mmol) was dissolved in dry diethyl
ether (20 mL) in 100 mL RB flask under an argon atmosphere. The reaction
was cooled to - 78 °C, tBuLi (11.25 mL, 1.60 M, 18.00 mmol) was added and
the reaction was stirred for 15 minutes. Then ZnBr2 (2.23 g, 9.90 mmol),
dissolved in dry diethyl ether was added, and the mixture was stirred at
-78 °C for 30 mins, followed by addition of ethyl glyoxylate (2.75 g,
13.50 mmol, 50% by wt, toluene solution). The reaction mixture was warmed
up to r. t. during overnight stirring, quenched with saturated aqueous
NH4Cl solution, and extracted with diethyl ether (3 x 30 mL). The organic
phases were combined, dried over anhydrous MgSO4 and concentrated in
vacuo to give crude product. Purification by silica gel column (10% EA/
Pet. Ether) gave 5a, yield 1.99 g, 81%. IR (neat) 3432 (br s), 2935 (m),
1733 (s), 1460 (m), 1372 (m), 1247 (m), 1083 (s), 826 (m) cm-1; 1H NMR δ
0.11 (s, 6H), 0.93 (s, 9H), 1.30 (t, J = 7.2 Hz, 3H), 2.99 (br s, 1H) ,
4.25 (q, J = 7.2 Hz, 2H), 4.28-4.48 (m, 2H) , 4.92 (d, J = 8.1 Hz, 1H) ,
5.40-5.53 (m, 1H) , 5.73-5.87 (m, 1H) ; 13C NMR δ 5.1, 14.1, 18.3, 25.9,
60.0, 62.0, 67.9, 126.6, 134.8, 173.5.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
