$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: 1-(4-Methoxyphenyl)-2-buten-1-ol (±)-2b.
Method B-2: Under a nitrogen atmosphere, to a solution of the carbonyl
compound (3.7 mmol) in THF (12 mL) was dropwise added 1-propenylmagnesium
bromide (5.5 mmol) at -78 °C. The reaction mixture was allowed to warm to
room temperature and stirred until the complete consumption of the
substrate. After quenching with sat. aq. NH4Cl, the organic materials
were extracted with EtOAc. The combined organic extract was washed with
brine, dried over MgSO4, and evaporated in vacuo. The residue was
purified by column chromatography (silica gel) to give (±)-2. starting
from p-anisaldehyde (500 mg, 3.7 mmol), 1-propenylmagnesium bromide (0.5
M in THF; 11.0 mL, 5.5 mmol), and THF (12 mL). After 4 h at room
temperature, work-up and column chromatography (hexanes/EtOAc = 10:1).
1-(4-Methoxyphenyl)-2-buten-1-ol (±)-2b; 23:77 mixture of (E)-2b (650 mg,
99 %); colorless oil.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, alternative preparation shown
