$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure A. Aldol Addition of Acetic
Acid to Aldehydes. To an oven-dried 10-mL round-bottomed flask under N2
was added CH2Cl2 (5.0 mL), acetic acid (57 μL, 60 mg, 0.996 mmol),
i-Pr2NEt (435 μL, 323 mg, 2.50 mmol), aldehyde (1.4 mmol), and TMSOTf
(400 μL, 491 mg, 2.21 mmol). NOTE: addition of TMSOTf to the reaction
mixture produces a mildly exothermic reaction on this scale. The reaction
was stirred at room temperature, and the colorless solution became pale
yellow. After 2 h, the reaction mixture was added to a 25-mL
round-bottomed flask with 10 mL EtOH (95%) and 5-10 drops trifluoroacetic
acid. The reaction mixture was concentrated by rotary evaporation. Flash
chromatography (10-50% EtOAc/hex). The pure product.
(4E)-3-Hydroxy-4-methyl-5-phenylpent-4-enoic acid (10) When General
Procedure A was followed using α-methylcinnamaldehyde (195 μL, 204 mg,
1.40 mmol), the title compound was prepared as an off-white solid (71%
yield). mp: 54-59 °C; IR (film) 3316, 3017, 2909, 2360, 1709, 1399, 1280,
1187, 1024, 916, 753, 688 cm-1; 1H NMR (500 MHz, CDCl3) 7.43-7.22 (m,
5H), 6.63 (s, 1H), 4.67 (dd, J = 4.7, 8.0 Hz, 1H), 2.80-2.70 (m, 2H),
1.92 (s, 3H); 13C NMR (125 MHz, CDCl3) δ 171.4, 137.8, 137.1, 129.0,
128.2, 126.7, 126.5, 73.5, 40.1, 13.7; HRMS (ESI): Exact mass calcd for
C12H14O3Na [M+Na]+, 229.0835. Found 229.0838.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM alternative preparation shown
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Acetic Acid Aldol Reactions in the Presence of Trimethylsilyl
Trifluoromethanesulfonate
