$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Treatment of 1,1-dimethylallene (1a) and SnCl2 with benzaldehyde (2a), in
a mixture of aqueous hydrochloric acid and DMF at ambient temperature in
the presence of PdCl2- (PPh3)2 (2 mol %), leads to the formation of
carbonyl allylation product 3a in 95% isolated yield (Scheme 1). The
reaction is completely regioselective, giving 3a as the sole product.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM regioselective, stereoselective
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Highly Regioselective and Stereoselective Allylation of Aldehydes via
Palladium-Catalyzed in Situ Hydrostannylation of Allenes
