$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: (E)-1-(4-Methoxyphenyl)-2-buten-1-ol (±)-2b.
Method A: Under a nitrogen atmosphere, to a solution of the carbonyl
compound (14 mmol) in THF (70 mL) was dropwise added the corresponding
Grignard or lithium reagents (21 mmol) at -78 °C. The reaction mixture
was allowed to warm to room temperature and stirred until the complete
consumption of the substrate. After quenching with sat. aq. NH4Cl, the
organic materials were extracted with EtOAc. The combined organic extract
was washed with brine, dried over MgSO4, and evaporated in vacuo. The
residue was purified by column chromatography (silica gel) to give (±)-1
or (±)-2. using crotonaldehyde (250 mg, 3.6 mmol), p-MeOC6H4Li generated
from p-MeOC6H4Br (1.00 g, 5.4 mmol) and n-BuLi (1.65 M in hexanes; 3.20
mL, 5.4 mmol), and THF (12 mL). After 2 h at room temperature, work-up
and column chromatography (hexanes/EtOAc = 5:1).
(E)-1-(4-Chlorophenyl)-2-buten-1-ol (±)-2c; (2.57 g, 98%); colorless oil.
1H NMR (500 MHz, CDCl3) δ: 7.33-7.28 (m, 4H), 5.76 (dq, J= 15.0, 6.0 Hz,
1H), 5.64 (ddd, J= 15.0, 7.0, 1.5 Hz, 1H), 5.14 (dd, J= 7.0, 3.5 Hz, 1H),
1.91-1.88 (m, 1H), 1.72 (d, J= 6.0 Hz, 3H). 13C NMR (125 MHz, CDCl3) δ:
141.7, 133.2, 133.1, 128.5, 128.1, 127.5, 74.5, 17.7. IR (CHCl3) ν: 3603
cm-1. HRMS (ESI) m/z calcd for C10H10Cl [M-OH]+: 165.0471. Found:
165.0482.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
