$DATUM (E)-6-(benzyloxy)hex-4-en-3-ol To a solution of aldehyde 8 (6.62 g, 37.6
mmol) in diethyl ether (120 mL) at 0 °C was added slowly a solution of
ethylmagnesium bromide (1 M in tetrahydrofuran, 45 mL) and stirred. The
reaction was quenched after 1 h with saturated ammonium chloride solution
(150 mL). The aqueous layer was extracted with ethyl acetate (3 × 50 mL).
The combined organic layers were dried over anhydrous sodium sulfate and
concentrated in vacuum. The crude product was purified by silica gel
chromatography to provide a colorless oil (6.67 g, 90 % yield). IR (neat)
3399, 2962, 2931, 2857, 1495, 1454, 1361, 1093, 969, 737 cm-1; 1H NMR
(400 MHz, CDCl3, δ) 7.36-7.25 (m, 5H), 5.82-5.72 (m, 2H), 4.52 (s, 2H),
4.03 (t, J = 8.4 Hz, 2H), 1.74 (s, 1H), 1.61-1.52 (m, 2H), 0.94 (t, J = 4
Hz, 3H); 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3, δ) 138.1, 135.8, 128.3, 127.7, 127.6,
127.2, 73.6, 72.1, 70.1, 29.9, 9.6.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Grignard reaction
