$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General nitroaldol reaction procedure To a
solution of the chiral ligand (28 mg, 0.075 mmol, 8 mol%) in toluene (1
ml) was added dimethylzinc (3 mmol, 1 M in heptane) at -50 °C under N2.
After 10 min, MeNO2 (570 mg, 9.4 mmol) was added in one portion followed
by the aldehyde (0.94 mmol). After 1 hour, the reaction temperature was
warmed to -15 °C and saturated NH4Cl solution was added upon completion
of the reaction. The mixture was warmed to room temperature, extracted
with CHCl3 and the combined organic phases were dried over anhydrous
MgSO4. The solvents were removed under reduced pressure and the residue
was purified by flash column chromatography (15% EtOAc in hexanes).
2-Nitro-1-phenylethanol 1 1-Nitro-4-phenyl-but-3-en-2-ol 5
Chromatographic purification (hexanes:ethyl acetate = 90: 10) gave 179 mg
(0.93 mmol, 98%, 82% ee) of a white solid. 1H NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3) δ =
2.92 (b, 1H); 4.48 (d, J = 6.1 Hz, 2H); 5.02 (m, 1H); 6.10 (dd, J = 6.4
Hz, 15.9 Hz, 1H), 6.77 (d, J = 15.9 Hz, 1H), 7.24-7.39 (5H, m). 13C NMR
(75 MHz, CDCl3) δ = 70.2, 80.5, 125.6, 127.4, 129.1, 129.4, 134.2, 136.2.
The ee was determined by HPLC on Chiralpak AD using EtOH:hexanes (10:90)
as the mobile phase, t1 = 18.7 min, t2 = 22.2, min, α = 1.18.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, ee=82%, Henry reaction
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Asymmetric Nitroaldol Reaction Catalyzed by a C2-Symmetric Bisoxazolidine
Ligand
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Liu, Shuanglong; Wolf, Christian
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Organic Letters (2008), 10(9), 1831-1834

