$DATUM 3-Hydroxy-2-methylene-5-phenyl-4-pentenenitrile (19h). Purification by
column chromatography (3:1 hexane/EtOAc) afforded a desired compound 19h
(162 mg, 87%) as a yellow oil. Spectral data were identical to those
previously reported.10 TLC: R f 0.18 (3:1 hexane/EtOAc). 1H-NMR (400 MHz,
CDCl3): δ 7.43-7.29 (m, 5H), 6.76 (d, 1H, J = 15.6 Hz), 6.22 (dd, 1H, J =
15.6, 6.8 Hz), 6.12 (d, 1H, J = 1.2 Hz), 6.05 (d, 1H, J = 1.2 Hz), 4.94
(m, 1H), 2.06 (brs, 1H, J = 4.4 Hz). 13C-NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3): δ 135.8,
133.9, 130.3, 128.9, 128.6, 127.0, 126.8, 125.6, 117.2, 73.0.
