$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Preparation of (1Z,3S*,4R*)-4-chloro-1-phenylnon-1-en-3-ol (7): To a cold
(-78 °C), stirred solution of iodostyrene (115 mg, 0.50 mmol) in THF (10
mL) was added n-butyllithium (2.0 M soln. in hexane, 275 μL, 0.55 mmol).
The resulting solution was stirred at -78 °C for 30 minutes. After this
time, a solution of 2-chloroheptanal (82 mg, 0.55 mmol) in THF (1.0 mL)
was then added in one portion at -78 °C and the resulting mixture was
stirred for an additional 30 minutes. Saturated aqueous NH4Cl (2 mL) was
then added, the mixture was diluted with ethyl acetate (10 mL) and the
phases were separated. The aqueous phase was extracted with ethyl acetate
(3 x 10 mL) and the combined organic phases were washed with brine (5
mL), dried (MgSO4) and concentrated to provide a crude yellow solid.
Purification of the crude product by flash chromatography (silica gel,
3:1 hexanes-ethyl acetate) afforded
(1Z,3S*,4R*)-4-chloro-1-phenylnon-1-en-3-ol (7) as a clear oil, yield
(111 mg, 88%). 1H NMR (600 MHz, CDCl3) δ: 7.37-7.35 (m, 4H), 7.29 (m,
1H), 6.76 (dd, 1H, J = 0.9, 11.4 Hz), 5.85 (dd, 1H, J = 9.0, 11.4 Hz),
4.63 (dddd, 1H, J = 0.9, 4.2, 7.8, 9.0 Hz), 4.11 (m, 1H), 2.22 (d, 1H, J
= 7.8 Hz), 1.66 (m, 2H), 1.51 (m, 1H), 1.26 (m, 5H), 0.91 (t, 3H, J = 7.2
Hz). 13C NMR (150 MHz, CDCl3) δ: 136.3, 134.5, 134.2, 129.8, 128.7,
128.5, 128.4, 127.6, 70.1, 68.6, 33.6, 31.2, 26.2, 22.5, 14.0. IR (neat):
3393, 2955, 2930, 2859 cm-1 Exact mass calcd. for C15H20Cl: 235.1254
(M-H2O); found: 235.1248 (M-H2O).
