$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: B.A solution of tert-butyl isocyanide (1.2
equiv, 1.0 M in CH2Cl2) was added to a solution of an aldehyde (1.0 M in
CH2Cl2 based on aldehyde), pyridine-N-oxide (0.1 equiv), SiCl4 (1.1
equiv) at -74 °C over 30 min via a syringe pump. After being stirred
further for the indicated time, dry MeOH (2.5 mL) was added dropwise to
the reaction mixture at -74 °C. After being stirred for 40 min at -74 °C,
the mixture was transferred dropwise to a Vigorously stirred, ice-cold,
saturated aqueous solution of NaHCO3 (20 mL) and stirred for 2 h further
at rt. The white precipitate was filtered off through Celite and the
filtrate was extracted with CH2Cl2 (4 x 20 mL). The combined organic
layers were dried (MgSO4) and concentrated under reduced pressure.
Pyridine-N-oxide was separated from the product by silica gel column
chromatography (hexane/EtOAc). Following General Procedure III B, a
solution of tert-butyl isocyanide (63 μL, d = 0.735, 0.6 mmol, 1.2 equiv)
in CH2Cl2 (0.5 mL) was added via a syringe pump to the cold solution of
trans-cinnamaldehyde 3g (63 μL, d = 1.048, 0.5 mmol), pyridine-N-oxide
(4.8 mg, 0.05 mmol, 0.1 equiv), SiCl4 (63 μL, d = 1.483, 0.55 mmol, 1.1
equiv) at -74 °C over 30 min. The mixture was stirred for 4 h at -74 °C.
Work-up with the methanol quench provided 71mg (74%) of (±)- 11 after
silica gel column chromatography (20 mm column, 60 g SiO2, Rf 0.25,
hexane/EtOAc, 3/1). Data for (±)-11: GC: (S)-11, tR 37.80 min (49.4%);
(R)-11, tR 38.54 min (50.6%) (Chiraldex BPH, 93 °C, 20 psi)
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Catalytic, Enantioselective α-Additions of Isocyanides: Lewis Base
Catalyzed Passerini-Type Reactions
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Denmark, Scott E.; Fan, Yu
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Journal of Organic Chemistry (2005), 70(24), 9667-9676

