$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 1-(furan-2-yl)but-3-en-1-ol ((+/-)-13): To a 1 M THF solution of furfural
(15 g, 156 mmol) was added a 2.0 M THF solution of allyl magnesium
chloride (78 mL, 156 mmol) under a nitrogen atmosphere at 0 °C . The
reaction mixture was allowed to slowly warm to room temperature and
stirred for 10 h, diluted with diethyl ether (200 mL), quenched with
saturated NaHSO4 (100 mL) and followed by saturated NaHCO3 (300 mL),
extracted with diethyl ether (2 x 400 mL). The combined organic layers
were washed with saturated NaHCO3 (200 mL), followed by brine (200 mL),
dried (Na2SO4) and concentrated in vacuo to give a light colored oil.
Flash chromatography afforded homoallyl alcohol (+/-)-13 (18.93 g, 137
mmol, 88%) as a colorless oil 1-(furan-2-yl)but-3-en-1-ol ((+/–)-13):
yield 88%. Rf (30 % ether/hexane) = 0.30; FTIR (thin film, cm-1) 3366,
1638. 1H NMR (200 MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.35 (d, J = 1.2 Hz, 1H), 6.32 (dd, J =
3.2, 1.2 Hz, 1H), 6.18 (d, J = 3.2 Hz, 1H), 5.85 (m, 1H), 5.00-5.17 (m,
2H), 4.76 (dd, J = 6.6, 6.6 Hz, 1H), 3.74 (br., 1H), 2.61 (t, J = 6.6 Hz,
2H); 13C NMR (75 MHz, CDCl3) 156.0, 141.9, 133.6, 118.3, 110, 106, 66.8,
40.0.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective
