$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: 2-methyl-1-(Tribromomethyl)cyclohexanol (1c):
To a -30 °C suspension consisting of Mg (146 mg, 6 mmol), ClCH2CH2Cl (8
mL), and TiCl4 (0.5 mL ,1 M in ClCH2CH2Cl, 0.5 mmol) was stirred for 1
min, then added a solution of 2-methyl cyclohexanone 1a (112 mg, 1 mmol)
and CHBr3 (1.5 mL) in ClCH2CH2Cl (2 mL). After being stirred for 10 min,
THF (1.5 mL) was added. The yellow-brown slurry was stirred for 2 h at
-30 °C and then saturated potassium carbonate solution (10 mL) and
dichloromethane (20 mL) were added . The mixture was warmed to 0 °C for
30 min and the phases were separated. The organic layer was dried over
MgSO4, filtered, and concentrated in vacuo. The product was purified by
flash chromatograph on silica gel with a 10-30% EtOAc:hexane gradient.
(E)-1,1,1-Tribromo-4-phenylbut-3-en-2-ol (17c): As described above, 132
mg (1 mmol) of 17a and Mg (6 mmol)/TiCl4 (0.5 mmol)/ClCH2CH2Cl (10
mL)/CHBr3 (1.5 mL)/THF (1.5 mL) gave a crude reaction mixture.
Purification by flash chromatography (silica gel, hexane:EtOAc). 329 mg
(86%) of 17c as a white solid. mp 177-180 °C; R f = 0.30 (hexane:EtOAc
10:1). IR (neat) : ν = 3460, 3009, 2965, 2923, 2869, 2844, 1650, 1602,
1485, 1435, 1420, 1256, 1211, 1059, 822, 763 cm-1; 1H NMR (400 MHz,
CDCl3) δ 7.46-7.43 (m, 2 H), 7.40-7.29 (m,3 H), 6.94 (d, J = 16 HZ, 1 H),
6.39 (dd, J = 16 HZ, 6 HZ, 1 H), 4.71-4.68 (m, 1 H), 3.08 (d, J = 6 HZ, 1
H); 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3) δ 136.66, 135.74, 128.71, 128.58, 126.90,
123.66, 84.61, 53.87; HRMS-EI calcd for C10H9Br3O: 381.8204. Found:
381.8210
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
