$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure II: Aldol Addition of (Z)-5:
(1R,2R,4S)-5-tert-Butyldimethylsilyloxy-2,4-dimethyl-1-hydroxy-1-phenyl-3-pentanone
(syn,syn-16a) Trichlorosilyl enol ether (Z)-5 (364 mg, 1.00 mmol) was
added to a solution of (R,R)-1a (37 mg, 0.10 mmol, 0.10 equiv) in 1.00 mL
of CH2Cl2. The reaction mixture was cooled to -78°C using an acetone/CO2
bath, and PhCHO (102 mL, 1.00 mmol, 1 equiv) was added by syringe. After
stirring for 6 h, the reaction mixture was quenched by pouring into a
vigorously stirred solution of cold, sat. aq. NaHCO3 solution. The
resulting slurry was stirred for 1 h and was filtered through Celite. The
layers were separated and the aqueous layer was extracted with 10 mL of
CH2Cl2. The organic phases were combined, washed with 2 mL of brine and
were dried (Na2SO4), filtered, and concentrated. The crude product was
purified by column chromatography (pentane/ether, 3/1, SiO2) to afford
241 mg (0.72 mmol, 72%) of 16a as a clear, viscous oil.
(2S,4S,5S)-1-Triisopropylsilyloxy-2,4-dimethyl-5-hydroxy-6-octen-3-one
(syn,anti-17d) Following General Procedure II from (Z)-6 (472 mg, 1.00
mmol), crotonaldehyde (83 mL, 1.00 mmol, 1.0 equiv), (S,S)-1a (37 mg,
0.10 mmol, 0.1 equiv) and TBAI (73.9 mg, 0.20 mmol, 0.2 equiv) in 1 mL of
CH2Cl2 for 6 h, was obtained 293 mg (0.85 mmol, 85%) of 17d as a clear,
colorless, viscous oil after column chromatography (pentane/ether, 3/1,
SiO2). The diastereomeric ratio was determined by 1H NMR integration of
HC(5). 1H NMR: (500 MHz, CDCl3) 5.72 (dq, J = 15.2, 6.4, 1 H, HC(7));
5.46 (dd, J = 15.1, 6.6, 1 H, HC(6)); 4.36 (m, 1 H, HC(5)); 3.91-3.63
(ABX, 2 H, H2C(1)); 2.99 (sext, J = 7.6, 1 H, HC(2)); 2.81 (qd, J = 7.0,
4.0, 1 H, HC(4)); 2.66 (d, J = 3.2, 1 H, HO); 1.70 (dd, J = 7.3, 0.7, 3
H, H3C(8)); 1.12 (d, J =7.1, 3 H, H3C(11)); 1.11 - 1.00 (m, 24 H,
H3C(10), H3C(12), HC(9)) 13C NMR: (126 MHz, CDCl3) 217.83 (C(3)); 130.85
(C(7)); 127.63 (C(6); 72.70 (C(1)); 65.82 (C(5)); 50.79 (C(4)); 48.24
(C(2)); 17.84 (C(10)); 17.62 (C(8)); 13.11 (C(11)); 11.75 (C(9)); 9.60
(C(12)) IR: (neat) 3468 (br, w); 2944 (m); 2868 (m); 1703 (m); 1462 (m);
1383 (w); 1250 (w); 1104 (m); 1068 (m) MS: (FI) 342.2 (M+, 1); 301.2 (6);
300.1 (23); 299.1 (100); 229.1 (15); 175.4 (7) Opt. Rot.: [α]D 24 + 81.7
(c = 0.35, EtOH) TLC: Rf 0.25 (pentane/ether, 3/1) [silica gel,
p-anisaldehyde] Analysis: C19H38O3Si (342.59) Calcd: C, 66.61; H, 11.18%
Found: C, 66.21; H, 11.13%
