$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure:
(1R,2R,5S)-5-tert-Butyldimethylsilyloxy-2-methyl-1-hydroxy-1-phenyl-3-hexanone
(syn,anti-11a). Trichlorosilyl enol ether (Z)-7 (364 mg, 1.00 mmol) was
added to a solution of (R,R)-20a (37 mg, 0.10 mmol, 0.10 equiv) in 1.00
mL of CH2Cl2. The reaction mixture was cooled to -78 °C and PhCHO (102
μL, 1.00 mmol, 1 equiv) was added by syringe. After stirring for 6 h, the
reaction mixture was quenched by pouring it into a vigorously stirring
solution of cold, sat. aq. NaHCO3 solution (15 mL). The resulting slurry
was stirred for 3 h and was filtered through Celite. The layers were
separated, and the aqueous layer was extracted with 20 mL of CH2Cl2. The
organic phases were combined, washed with 5 mL of brine and were dried
(Na2SO4), filtered, and concentrated. The crude product was purified by
column chromatography (pentane/ether, 3/1, SiO2).
(2S,5S,6S)-2-Triisopropylsilyloxy-5-methyl-6-hydroxy-7-nonen-4-one
(syn,syn-12d). Yield: 285 mg (0.83 mmol, 83%) of 12d as a clear,
colorless, viscous oil. Data for (syn,syn)-12d: 1H NMR: (500 MHz,
benzene-d6) 5.58 (dqd, J=15.4, 6.4, 1.2, 1 H, HC(8)); 5.35 (ddd, J=15.4,
6.1, 1.7, 1 H, HC(7)); 4.51 (sext, J=5.9, 1 H, HC(2)); 4.25 (m, 1 H,
HC(6)); 2.68-2.34 (ABX, 2 H, H2C(3)); 2.38 (m, 1 H, HC(5)); 2.00 (d,
J=3.4, 1 H, HO); 1.51 (dd, J=6.4, 1.0, 3 H, H3C(9)); 1.18 (d,J=6.1, 3 H,
H3C(1)); 1.16-1.00 (m, 21 H, H3C(11), HC(10)); 1.05 (d, J=7.1, 3 H,
H3C(12)) 13C NMR: (126 MHz, CDCl3) 213.71 (C(4)); 130.57 (C(7)); 127.97
(C(8); 72.41 (C(6)); 64.95 (C(2)); 52.15 (C(3)); 51.56 (C(5)); 24.04
(C(1)); 17.97 (C(11)); 17.66 (C(9)); 12.30 (C(11)); 10.36 (C(12)) IR:
(neat) 3441 (br, m); 2963 (s); 2944 (m); 2893 (m); 2867 (s); 1710 (m);
1462 (m); 1375 (m); 1132 (m); 1109 (m); 1013 (m) MS: (FI) 343.2 (2);
342.2 (M+, 3); 301.2 (7); 300.2 (22); 299.2 (100); 229.2 (37); 175.3 (5)
Opt. Rot.: [α]24D + 30.4 (c = 0.54, EtOH) TLC: Rf 0.16 (pentane/ether,
3/1) [silica gel, p-anisaldehyde] Analysis: C19H38O3Si (342.59) Calcd: C,
66.61; H, 11.18% Found: C, 66.33; H, 11.33%.
