$DATUM General/Typical Procedure:
(1R,2R,5S)-5-tert-Butyldimethylsilyloxy-2-methyl-1-hydroxy-1-phenyl-3-hexanone
(syn,anti-11a). Trichlorosilyl enol ether (Z)-7 (364 mg, 1.00 mmol) was
added to a solution of (R,R)-20a (37 mg, 0.10 mmol, 0.10 equiv) in 1.00
mL of CH2Cl2. The reaction mixture was cooled to -78 °C and PhCHO (102
μL, 1.00 mmol, 1 equiv) was added by syringe. After stirring for 6 h, the
reaction mixture was quenched by pouring it into a vigorously stirring
solution of cold, sat. aq. NaHCO3 solution (15 mL). The resulting slurry
was stirred for 3 h and was filtered through Celite. The layers were
separated, and the aqueous layer was extracted with 20 mL of CH2Cl2. The
organic phases were combined, washed with 5 mL of brine and were dried
(Na2SO4), filtered, and concentrated. The crude product was purified by
column chromatography (pentane/ether, 3/1, SiO2).
(2S,5R,6R)-2-Triisopropylsilyloxy-5-methyl-6-hydroxy-7-nonen-4-one
(syn,anti-12d). Yield: 272 mg (0.79 mmol, 79%) of 12d as a clear,
colorless, viscous oil. Data for (syn,anti)-12d: 1H NMR: (500 MHz,
benzene-d6) 5.61 (dqd, J=15.2, 6.4, 1.2, 1 H, HC(8)); 5.37 (ddd, J=15.4,
6.1, 1.5, 1 H, HC(7)); 4.51 (sext, J=6.3, 1 H, HC(2)); 4.31 (m, 1 H,
HC(6)); 2.68-2.34 (ABX, 2 H, H2C(3)); 2.36 (m, 1 H, HC(5)); 2.10 (d,
J=3.5, 1 H, HO); 1.53 (d, J=6.5, 3 H, H3C(9)); 1.17 (d,J=6.1, 3 H,
H3C(1)); 1.15-1.03 (m, 21 H, H3C(11), HC(10)); 1.01 (d, J=7.3, 3 H,
H3C(12)) 13C NMR: (126 MHz, CDCl3) 214.08 (C(4)); 130.48 (C(7)); 127.87
(C(8); 72.16 (C(6)); 65.15 (C(2)); 52.07 (C(3)); 51.63 (C(5)); 24.09
(C(1)); 18.02 (C(11)); 17.67 (C(9)); 12.32 (C(10)); 10.19 (C(12)) IR:
(neat) 3442 (br, m); 2963 (s); 2943 (s); 2893 (s); 2868 (s); 1710 (s);
1463 (m); 1375 (m); 1130 (s); 1102 (m); 1013 (s) MS: (FI) 343.2 (M+, 3);
301.2 (7); 300.2 (22); 299.6 (4); 299.2 (100); 281.2 (4); 272.2 (8);
230.1 (6); 29.1 (36); 176.2 (3); 176.1 (4); 176.0 (4); 175.9 (5); 175.8
(6); 175.6 (6); 175.4 (5); 175.3 (5); 175.1 (4) Opt. Rot.: [α]24D-15.9 (c
= 0.54, EtOHc = 0.54) TLC: Rf 0.16 (pentane/ether, 3/1) [silica gel,
p-anisaldehyde] Analysis: C19H38O3Si (342.59) Calcd: C, 66.61; H, 11.18%
Found: C, 66.37; H, 11.36%.
