$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure D: Allyl additions. The
aldehyde (1.20 mmol) was added to a stirred solution of allylboronic
esters 8, 9, 19 or 20 (1.00 mmol) in dry CH2Cl2 (0.5 mL) at 0°C under a
dry nitrogen atmosphere. The mixture was stirred and allowed to warm to
room temperature overnight. After complete consumption of allylboronic
ester (as judged by TLC, 3-15 d), the solvents were removed under reduced
pressure. The residue was dissolved in THF (10 mL) and LiAlH4 (4.00 mmol)
was added. After 1 h, the mixture was diluted with Et2O (10 mL), cooled
to 0°C and treated successively with H2O (184 μL), 15% aqueous NaOH (184
μL) and H2O (544 μL). The solids were filtered off, washed thoroughly
with Et2O and the filtrate dried over anhydrous MgSO4. Filtration and
removal of the solvents under reduced pressure completed the process. The
product was then subjected to flash-column chromatography on silica gel
(petroleum ether/ethyl acetate, 60:40) yielding 1,5-diols.
(1R,5S,2E)-1,5-Dicyclohexylpent-2-ene-1,5-diol (ent-17jj) and
(1R,5R,2Z)-1,5-Dicyclohexylpent-2-ene-1,5-diol (ent-18jj). Yield 89%.
[α]D20 = -11.13 (c 1.02, CHCl3); Mosher ester: ee > 95%; [α]D 20 = +29.61
(c 1.09, CHCl3).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Palladium-catalyzed synthesis of enantiomerically pure α-substituted
allylboronic esters and their addition to aldehydes
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Fernandez, Enrique; Pietruszka, Joerg; Frey, Wolfgang
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Journal of Organic Chemistry (2010), 75(16), 5580-5589

