$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Typical Procedure for Zn(HMDS)2-Catalyzed
Propargylation of Carbonyl Compounds 2a-t with Allenylboronate 1b
Zn(HMDS)2 (0.0012 mmol) was dissolved in freshly distilled dry THF (0.2
mL), then the solution was keep in 15 or 25°C (depending on the
substrates). To this solution was added a solution of allenylboronate 1
(0.600 mol) in freshly distilled dry THF (0.4 mL). After stirring for 10
min, the solution of 2 (0.40 mmol) in freshly distilled dry THF (0.4 mL)
was then slowly added during 12 h. The mixture was then stirred at this
temperature for another 24 h. Finally, the reaction was quenched by
saturated aqueous NH4Cl, and the resultant mixture was extracted by EtOAc
(10 mL*3). The combined organic layer was dried over anhydrous Na2SO4.
The solution was evaporated in vacuum, and the residue was purified by
silica-gel column chromatography or preparative thin-layer
chromatography. The desired product as mixture of allenylic/propargyl
alcohols. 2-(4-Methoxyphenyl)penta-3,4-dien-2-ol (3b)
1-(Furan-2-yl)buta-2,3-dien-1-ol (3s) 13 1-(furan-2-yl)but-3-yn-1-ol (4s)
3s: 1H NMR (CDCl3, 600 MHz) δ 7.40 (m, 1H), 6.34-6.30 (m, 2H), 5.54-5.51
(m, 1H), 5.26 (m, 1H), 4.99-4.94 (m, 2H), 2.36 (s, 1H); 13C NMR (CDCl3,
150 MHz) δ 207.6, 154.9, 142.4, 110.2, 106.6, 92.1, 78.6, 65.6. 4s: 1H
NMR (CDCl3, 500 MHz) δ 7.39 (br, 1H), 6.35 (m, 2H), 4.88 (br, 1H), 2.78
(m, 2H), 2.50 (br, 1H), 2.08 (m, 1H). 13C NMR (CDCl3, 151 MHz) δ 154.6,
142.3, 110.3, 106.7, 79.9, 71.2, 66.1, 26.1. IR (neat): ν = 3293, 2919,
2121, 1957, 1727, 1680, 1613, 1503, 1425 cm-1; HRMS (DART) calcd. for
C8H7O+ [M-OH]+: 119.0497, found: 119.0499.
