$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: (13) The typical procedure for the catalytic
Ni/Cr-mediated coupling is given below. To a suspension of 5 (0.8 mg,
0.0020 mmol), 4 (0.3 mg, 0.0010 mmol), LiCl (17 mg, 0.40 mmol), manganese
powder (22 mg, 0.40 mmol), and Zr(Cp)2Cl2 (58 mg, 0.20 mmol) in DME (0.30
mL) were added 1 (27 μL, 0.20 mmol) and 2 (84 mg, 0.4 mmol). The mixture
was stirred for 4 h at room temperature under nitrogen, diluted with
ethyl acetate (10 mL), filtered, and concentrated under reduced pressure.
The residue was purified by silica gel flash column chromatography
(elution with hexanes/ethyl acetate ) 19/1 to 9/1) to give 3 (39 mg, 90%)
as colorless oil.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
