$DATUM Enantio- and Diastereoselective Vinyl Additions to Aldehydes. General
Procedure. An oven-dried 10 mL Schlenk flask that had been thoroughly
purged with N2 was charged with trisvinyl borane (0.4 equiv, 0.4 M in
toluene) and cooled to - 10 °C. Me2Zn (1.4 equiv, 2 M in toluene) was
added dropwise over 10 min and allowed to stirred at this temperature for
10 min before the addition of (−)-MIB (4 mol%). The reaction was warmed
to 0 °C and a solution of aldehyde (1 equiv, 1 M in toluene) was added
over 30 min with the aid of a syringe pump. The reaction was allowed to
stir at this temperature for 12 hours and was quenched with ~100 μL H2O.
After stirring for 15 min, MgSO4 was added followed by 5 mL of diethyl
ether.The resulting suspension was filtered, and successively washed with
diethyl ether (~5 mL × 2). The organic layer was concentrated and
chromatographed on silica gel that had been pretreated with triethylamine
(2.5% v/v Et3N) to afford the desired product .
3-Ethoxy-1-phenyl-prop-2-en-1-ol (S1). The General Procedure was applied
to benzaldehyde on 1.0 mmol (106.1 mg, 1 M in toluene) scale. The crude
product was purified by column chromatography on silica gel that had been
pretreated with triethylamine (2.5 % v/v Et3N, 20 % ethyl acetate in
hexanes) to afford the desired product as colorless oil (175 mg, 98 %
yield). colorless oil. [α]D 20 = +18.4 (c 1.00, MeOH); 1H NMR (C6D6, 500
MHz): δ 0.96 (t, 3H, J = 7.0 Hz), 1.52 (br, 1H), 3.19-3.31 (m, 2H),
4.87-4.92 (m, 2H), 6.36-6.42 (m, 1H), 7.08-7.12 (m, 1H), 7.18-7.22 (m,
2H), and 7.41- 7.43 (m, 2H) ppm. 13C{1H} NMR (C6D6, 125 MHz): δ 14.6,
64.3, 72.6, 107.8, 126.3, 127.3, 128.5, 145.1, and 148.9 ppm. IR (neat):
3400, 1650, 1603, 1493, 1478, 1454, and 1394 cm-1. HRMS calcd for C11H13O
(M – OH)+: 161.0967, found 161.0972.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
